 if(attempted==0)'- CellChat installation is authorized and completed; inference is being prepared or is in progress. Latest per-sample statuses are reported above.' else '- Per-sample complete objects, runtimes, errors and warnings are listed in 02_cellchat_per_sample/sample_run_status.tsv. Early data.table export/runner errors were retained in attempt archives and repaired from complete native objects; no inferential parameters were changed and no failed inference was recoded as zero. The first sample was rerun once before object preservation was added; subsequent export repairs reused the complete native objects.',
 '', '## Explicit sample-edge consensus','', '- source and target >=30 cells -> structurally eligible. Undetected communication in a successful eligible sample -> weight=0. Ineligible -> NA. Inference failure -> NA plus FAILED, never weight=0.', '- For complete evaluable edges: n_eligible=sum(eligible); n_detected=sum(weight>0 over eligible); prevalence=n_detected/n_eligible; consensus_strength=median(all eligible weights including real zeros). QC includes mean, IQR, median nonzero and maximum.', '- Primary display rule is exactly n_eligible>=3 and prevalence>=0.30. Non-retained display entries are zero; all audit rows remain. Edges passing this rule can still have median=0 and thus no visible line.', '- If an eligible sample failed, complete-cohort median/prevalence are unknown. Such edges retain n_missing_eligible, observed median, and prevalence bounds; incomplete edges are not displayed. This avoids both false zeros and silently redefining the eligible denominator.',paste0('- Structural eligible sample-edge observations=',sum(cfg$eligibility$eligible),'.'),
 if(consensus_exists)paste0('- Rule-retained edges=',sum(stats$retained),'; positive edges drawn=',sum(stats$display_strength>0),'; incomplete edges=',sum(stats$n_missing_eligible>0),'.') else '- Retained edges, prevalence distribution and strongest signals are NOT AVAILABLE before inference.',
 '', '## Strongest overall relationships','',markdown_table(edge_top('all')),'','## Strongest fibro outgoing relationships','',markdown_table(edge_top('out')),'','## Strongest fibro incoming relationships','',markdown_table(edge_top('in')),'',
 '## NicheNet pre-flight and planned mechanism prioritization','', '- The user corrected NicheChat to NicheNet/nichenetr on 2026-10-08. NICHECHAT_STATUS=NOT_APPLICABLE; previous name-audit requirements are revoked. Historical audit files are archived, not used as computation prerequisites.', markdown_table(nn_summary),'',markdown_table(nn_compat),'','- Official saeyslab/nichenetr is used for ligand prioritization against a receiver transcriptional program; no second 14x14 network is constructed.', paste0('- Current NicheNet state: ',nn_status,'. See 05_nichenet_preflight/NicheNet_preflight_audit.md for installed version, commit, resource checksum and symbol compatibility.'), '- Sender: frozen Fibro_C0–C6. Candidate receivers: Epithelial, Myeloid, Endothelial, T_NK and other major populations with stable CellChat support.', '- Per-sample sender ligand and receiver receptor expression are audited from the unchanged RNA/data layer. Expression is detection>0; sample/group eligibility stays >=30; no expression cutoff is silently promoted to biological proof.', '- geneset_oi is NOT DEFINED. Ligand activity, ligand-target inference and cross-method high-confidence mechanism calls are NOT RUN. A documented, sample-aware receiver program is required first; no stage comparison or arbitrary top-DEG set is used.', '- CellChat-prioritized fibro→receiver pairs are saved as follow-up candidates, with their exact LR complex definitions and expression gates. This is preparation, not evidence of NicheNet ligand activity.', '- Expected future candidate evidence: stable CellChat support + sender ligand expression + receiver receptor expression + high NicheNet activity + interpretable downstream receiver targets. These evidence types remain separate.',
